<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Govinda III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 793–814</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Govinda III was a king of the Rashtrakuta dynasty of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>, the son of Dhruva. He led campaigns as far north as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and the Himalayan foothills, defeating the Gurjara-Pratihara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagabhata-ii">Nagabhata II</a> and receiving the submission of the Pala ruler Dharmapala. In the south he subdued the Pallavas and other Tamil rulers, bringing Rashtrakuta power to its greatest extent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/govinda-iii.jpg" alt="Govinda III" width="246" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B. Lewis Rice (Benjamin Lewis Rice, 1837-1927) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inscription_of_Rashtrakuta_Emperor_Govinda_III_at_Veerabhadra_temple,_Mavali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
